## Project Structure

```
.cursor/            # Cursor-native config: agents/, rules/, mcp.json
.space/             # Mission state
  missions/<id>/    # spec.md, plan.json, mission.json, evidence.jsonl
  archive/          # Shipped missions
  roadmaps/         # Roadmap files (*.json)
```

## Branches

`feat/<id>/<title>` -- one branch per feature. Never write on `main`.

## Commits

Conventional Commits (feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, test:, refactor:). Target 1-3 per branch, max 5. Squash WIP before merge. Rebase on `main` -> verify -> `git merge --no-ff`.

## Mission IDs

`M07FYB5W5` -- compact sortable (prefix + base36 ms since 2026-01-01).

Generate with: `node -e "const MS=Date.now()-new Date('2026-01-01').getTime();console.log('M'+MS.toString(36).toUpperCase())"`

## Mission Artifacts

### mission.json
```json
{
  "id": "<mission-id>",
  "title": "<title>",
  "state": "active|ready|blocked|shipped",
  "branches": ["<branch-name>"],
  "createdAt": "<iso-date>"
}
```

### plan.json
```json
{
  "planName": "<short-name>",
  "missionId": "<mission-id>",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "title": "<imperative>",
      "status": "pending|in_progress|done|blocked",
      "files": ["<path>"],
      "acceptance": ["<check>"],
      "verify": "<command>",
      "evidence": ["<label>"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### spec.md
Markdown file describing what and why. Free-form.

### evidence.jsonl
JSON Lines file. Each line is one evidence entry:
```json
{"label":"<label>","command":"<command>","output":"<output>","ts":"<iso-timestamp>"}
```

### Roadmap (.space/roadmaps/<id>.json)
```json
{
  "id": "<uuid-or-slug>",
  "title": "<title>",
  "description": "<description>",
  "missions": [
    {"id": "<mission-id>", "description": "<brief>"}
  ],
  "issues": [
    {"number": 1, "title": "...", "url": "https://...", "state": "open", "phase": "mvp|polish|ship"}
  ],
  "createdAt": "<iso-date>",
  "updatedAt": "<iso-date>"
}
```
Roadmap ID format: lowercase kebab-case slug derived from title (e.g. "add-user-auth").

### GitHub Issue Reference
When creating issues from roadmap, link them by adding to the roadmap's `issues` array.
When discovering bugs during any lane, create a GitHub issue with `gh issue create`:
```
gh issue create --title "<title>" --body "<body>" --label bug
```
Then append issue to roadmap: read roadmap JSON, add to `issues` array, write back.

## Evidence Capture

Capture evidence with `spacecraft evi`:
```
spacecraft evi <label> -- <command>
# or with explicit mission:
spacecraft evi --mission <id> <label> -- <command>
```

This runs the command, captures stdout, and appends a properly-escaped JSONL line to `.space/missions/<id>/evidence.jsonl`.

Command output in evidence.jsonl must be actual captured output -- never fabricated.

## Standards

- Never use the em dash ("-"). Use plain dash instead.
- Never manually modify CHANGELOG.md or any auto-generated files.
- Bug fixes: reproduce in E2E setting as close to end-user experience as possible before fixing.
- Lint, test failures, and test flakiness get fixed even if not caused by current work.

## Git Safety

- Check dirty tree before edits. Work with user changes; do not revert unrelated changes.
- If workspace is not a git worktree, stop before editing product files unless user has accepted no-git risk.
- Before code or dependency changes, check official current docs/registry/releases.
- Run `git branch --show-current` to verify you are on a feature branch before any code edits.
